sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2023-glue-05> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Bioelectric networks, through their plasticity, multiscale historicity (memory) and learning capacity, act as a 'cognitive glue' that binds the cybernetic goal-directedness of single cells into a higher-order system pursuing larger-scale goals (a larger cognitive light cone), and this capacity is not unique to brains.";
    dc:type "mechanism";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Bioelectric networks are a cognitive glue that enlarges the cognitive light cone of cells";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Levin M, “Bioelectric networks: the cognitive glue enabling evolutionary scaling from physiology to mind”, Animal cognition (2023), doi:10.1007/s10071-023-01780-3; section “Bioelectricity: the ancient cognitive glue”. Scope: Neural and non-neural cell collectives in multicellular organisms"
}
